# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> concurrent PRs
# add distinct files instead of editing run_gates.sh's shared registry.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail] [timeout]
register_gate "tests/test_graph_extract_isolation.py" "GRAPH EXTRACTION ISOLATION GATE: PASS" "graph extraction child isolation, deadline, cleanup, and DB-preservation contract" "graph extraction isolation: full/incremental repository work runs in a secret-free fresh exec child under one shared deadline and one process slot; real FIFO parser blocking is killed and synchronously reaped with no surviving PID; a rare slow post-kill reap retains the slot and remains content-free health-visible after event inflight clears, then fails at an absolute replacement bound if its daemon never returns; a configured long parser allowance applies only to background owners, while event owners retain the worker bound even under a 900s override; timeout performs no DB graph write and never multiplies incremental into full; only deterministic archive/file/output/memory caps may store honest Unknown" "GRAPH EXTRACTION ISOLATION: a poison repository cannot wedge the worker pool or erase a healthy graph; kill cleanup is bounded, an unkillable event child cannot leave Render health green beyond the worker bound, and valid long-running background configuration does not cause a false restart" 40 30
